  "solution": {
    "text": "Number of moles of HCl <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.1</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>40</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.004</mn></math><br />Number of moles of NaOH <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">M</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">V</mi></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.45</mn><mo>×</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>1000</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.0045</mn></math><br />Remaining moles of NaOH after neutralization = 0.0045 – 0.004 = 0.0005<br />Molarity of <math><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">O</mi><msup><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">H</mi></mrow><mrow><mo>-</mo></mrow></msup></math> <math><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>0.0005</mn></mrow><mrow><mn>50</mn></mrow></mfrac><mo>×</mo><mn>1000</mn><mo>=</mo><mn>0.01</mn><mtext>M</mtext></math><br />So pOH <math><mo>=</mo><mn>2</mn></math><br />So pH = 14 – 2 = 12",
